SUMMARY:🍁🌿 Fall Hike: East Don Trail Adventure 🍪🥾
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 15 Years!\n# **Tor
 onto’s Newest Ravine Trail\, Autumn Scenery & Fresh-Baked Cookies!**\n\n
 Did you join us for our last East Don Trail adventure? People had such a g
 reat time\, and there was plenty to talk about afterward! Now that fall is
  here\, we’re heading back to enjoy the trail in autumn.\nJoin us as we 
 explore the **East Don Trail**\, one of Toronto’s newest additions to it
 s incredible ravine system.\n\nThis beautiful route follows the East Don R
 iver through peaceful forests\, wetlands\, and scenic valley landscapes\, 
 connecting communities that were once separated.\nIf you’ve walked the L
 ower Don Trail\, this is a different experience.\n\nExpect quieter pathway
 s\, river views\, new bridges\, and the feeling of discovering another cor
 ner of Toronto that many people have yet to explore.\n\nMost of the route 
 is paved and relatively easy to walk. Just one warning: what goes down mus
 t come up! 😄\n\nThe final section includes a fairly steep hill\, so you
  should be comfortable tackling a good climb near the end.\nAnd the best p
 art? We’ll finish with a couple of optional stops for coffee\, baked goo
 ds\, and cookies!\n\n## 🚶‍♂️ What We’ll Do\n\nWe’ll meet outs
 ide Broadview Subway Station before making our way into the Don Valley to 
 explore the East Don Trail.\n\nAlong the way\, we’ll:\n🌿 Walk beside 
 the East Don River\n🌉 Cross bridges and follow scenic pathways\n🍂 En
 joy the ravine scenery and fall colours\n📸 Stop for photos and conversa
 tion\n☕ Visit Circles & Squares Bakery Café near the end of the trail\n
 🍪 Continue to the Peak Freans Cookie Outlet for discounted cookies and 
 treats\n\n**Both stops afterward are optional.** At Circles & Squares Bake
 ry Café\, you can grab a quick coffee or something baked\, or stay a litt
 le longer if you’d like. You’re welcome to join us for the cookie outl
 et afterward\, or make your own plans.\n\nWe’ll finish at **Coxwell Subw
 ay Station via TTC bus**. This is a one-way walk\, so we will not be retur
 ning to Broadview Station.\n\n## 🍁 Weather & Expectations\n\nThis walk 
 happens rain or shine unless severe weather makes it unsafe.\nThe trail is
  mostly paved and relatively easy\, but there is one fairly steep hill nea
 r the end. Please come prepared for that final climb and wear comfortable 
 walking shoes.\n\nThis is a social walk\, not a guided historical tour. We
 ’re here to enjoy the scenery\, have conversations\, and explore one of 
 Toronto’s newest green spaces together.\n\n## 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n
 📍 **Meeting location:** Outside Broadview Subway Station\n🦌 **Look f
 or:** My Moose Hat!\n⏰ **Meeting time:** 11:00 AM\n🚶 **Departure:** 1
 1:05 AM sharp. I’ll wait a maximum of five minutes.\n**Early is on time.
  On time is late.**\nPlease arrive on time\, as we’ll leave promptly.\n\
 n🏁 **End point:** Coxwell Subway Station\, via TTC bus.\n\n## ☕🍪 A
 fter the Walk\n\n### First stop: Circles & Squares Bakery Café\n\nWe’ll
  stop at **Circles & Squares Bakery Café** near the end of the trail. If 
 you’d like\, grab a coffee\, a pastry\, or something else from the baker
 y. This is a casual stop\, so there’s no obligation to buy anything or s
 tay for long.\n\n### Next stop: Peak Freans Cookie Outlet\n\nThen we’ll 
 head to the **Peak Freans Cookie Outlet**\, where you can browse their sel
 ection of cookies\, crackers\, and other treats at outlet prices.\nYou’r
 e welcome to join us for both stops\, just one\, or head home after the hi
 ke. The choice is yours!\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$5 cash in person o
 r by e-transfer to [mathewmaclean@hotmail.com](mailto:mathewmaclean@hotmai
 l.com).**\nThis fee helps support the group and allows us to continue orga
 nizing events like this. Thank you for supporting our community! 💛\n\n#
 # 🎒 What to Bring\n\n* 💧 Water\n* 👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n* 
 🧥 Weather-appropriate clothing\n* 📱 A phone or camera for photos\n* 
 💵 Spending money if you’d like coffee\, baked goods\, or cookies\n\n#
 # 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis group is open to anyone who wants to be so
 cial and make friends\, whether single or partnered.\nWe also organize mov
 ies\, walks and hikes\, arts and culture outings\, restaurant gatherings\,
  and plenty more. There’s always something happening!\n\n## ⚠️ A Few
  Reminders\n\n* You’re welcome to RSVP ahead of time or show up on the d
 ay if you’re unsure about your schedule.\n* Please keep an eye on the ev
 ent page for updates in case plans change or the event needs to be cancell
 ed.\n* Remember that this is a one-way walk ending at Coxwell Subway Stati
 on\, not Broadview.\n\n👤 **Organized by Mathew**\nQuestions? Post on th
 e event wall or email **[torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com](mailto:toron
 tomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com)**.\n\n**Come for Toronto’s newest trail.
 **\n**Stay for the coffee and cookies.**\n**Leave having discovered anothe
 r hidden corner of the city.** 🍁🌿🍪
